New Date Time API
New Date Time APINew Date Time APIJava 8 introduced a new Date Time API which is thread safe, zone ready and multiple direct methods to handle date operations.
Earlier date-time API was not thread safe and in concurrency issues could pop up while working with dates.
New date time APIs are using immutable constructs and no setter method thus making API more secure. The new API is designed considering zone, domain specific requirements.

Java 8 introduces a new date-time API under the package java.time. Following are some of the important classes introduced in java.time package.
Local − Simplified date-time API with no complexity of timezone handling.
Zoned − Specialized date-time API to deal with various timezones.